  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "In London, a special screening of the film took place on 1 November 2026.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383775061:107"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "According to India Today, reported on 2 November, Indian advance sales had reached approximately ₹46 crore, with the opening day accounting for ₹25.39 crore.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383775061:152"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "Directed by Nitesh Tiwari, who co-wrote the screenplay with Shridhar Raghavan, Ramayana: Part 1 is a 2026 Indian Hindi-language epic mythological film.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383775061:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "Ramayana: Part 1 stars Ranbir Kapoor, Yash, Sai Pallavi and Sunny Deol among others, with music by Hans Zimmer and A. R. Rahman.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1383775061:starring",
        "wiki:box:1383775061:music"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "It was released on 27 October 2026 at the Academy Museum, and worldwide on 5 November 2026.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1383775061:released"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:43Z",
      "text": "Principal photography began in Film City, Mumbai, and on 30 April the second schedule commenced in Mumbai.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:film:1383775061:1",
        "wiki:film:1383775061:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:51Z",
      "text": "The article places the filming in Film City, Ayodhya and Mumbai, with a specially constructed Ayodhya set serving as the primary filming location.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:film:1383775061:1",
        "wiki:film:1383775061:2",
        "wiki:film:1383775061:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:01:01Z",
      "text": "Birthplaces are on record for 6 of the people credited, and 5 of them were born in India.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q108560:P19",
        "wd:Q16908467:P19",
        "wd:Q20081051:P19",
        "wd:Q7296622:P19",
        "wd:Q76364:P19",
        "wd:Q944546:P19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:01:09Z",
      "text": "Hans Zimmer was born further afield, in Frankfurt, Germany.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q76364:P19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:01:19Z",
      "text": "On 2 November 2026, 60,024 people read the English article, about 8× the usual daily figure.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:Ramayana:_Part_1:2026-11-02",
        "views:en:Ramayana:_Part_1:prior"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:01:25Z",
      "text": "The article was read in 10 languages, and after English the most readers were on Hindi Wikipedia, with 2,219.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:Ramayana:_Part_1:2026-11-02",
        "views:hi:रामायणम्_(2026_फिल्म):2026-11-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:01:31Z",
      "text": "On the globe, each language glows where it is mainly spoken, brighter for more readers; a language is not a country.",
      "cites": [
        "views:hi:रामायणम्_(2026_फिल्म):2026-11-02",
